  "question": {
    "text": "A capacitor of capacitance $C$ is charged to a potential V. The flux of the electric field through a closed surface enclosing the positive plate of the capacitor is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{C V}{2 \\varepsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2 \\mathrm{CV}}{\\varepsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{CV}}{\\varepsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<br />Zero",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "From the Gauss's law<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />& \\phi=\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_{\\text {in }}}{\\epsilon_0}=\\frac{\\mathrm{Q}}{\\epsilon_0} \\quad \\because \\mathrm{Q}=\\mathrm{CV} \\\\<br />& \\therefore \\phi=\\frac{\\mathrm{CV}}{\\epsilon_0}<br />\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}